\" value=\"\" data-type=\"email\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-email-field kb-field-1\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-2 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\">Mobile Number<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_2\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\" data-label=\"Mobile Number\" type=\"tel\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"tel\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-tel-field kb-field-2\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-3 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\"><a href=\"/blog/what-is-court\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Court\">Court</a> to Appear in <span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_3\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\" data-label=\"Court to Appear in \" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"text\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-text-field kb-field-3\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-4 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\">Case Related to<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><textarea name=\"kb_field_4\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\" data-label=\"Case Related to\" type=\"textarea\" placeholder=\"\" data-type=\"textarea\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-textarea-field kb-field-4\" rows=\"1\" data-required=\"yes\"></textarea></div><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_id\" value=\"7744_eacc90-ec\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_post_id\" value=\"7744\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"kb_process_ajax_submit\"/><label class=\"kadence-verify-label\">Email<input class=\"kadence-blocks-field verify\" type=\"text\" name=\"_kb_verify_email\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" aria-hidden=\"true\" placeholder=\"Email\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-1p-ignore=\"true\" data-lpignore=\"true\" /></label><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-submit-field kb-field-desk-width-100\"><button class=\"kb-forms-submit button kb-button-size-standard kb-button-width-auto\">Connect me with a Attorney</button></div></form></div>\n<noscript><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-message kadence-blocks-form-warning\">Please enable JavaScript in your browser to submit the form</div><style>.kadence-form-7744_eacc90-ec .kadence-blocks-form-field.kb-submit-field { display: none; }</style></noscript></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>Are you familiar with the Newport News Circuit Court? Whether you’re a resident of Virginia or simply curious about the state’s judicial system, it’s important to understand the role and responsibilities of this court. In this article, we’ll provide an overview of the Newport News Circuit Court, including its history, structure, and key functions.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Understanding Virginia’s Court System</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Before delving into the specifics of the Newport News Circuit Court, it’s helpful to have a basic understanding of Virginia’s court system as a whole. Virginia’s judicial branch is divided into several different types of courts, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Circuit Courts</li>\n\n\n\n<li>General District Courts</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Juvenile and Domestic Relations District Courts</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Virginia Court of Appeals</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Supreme Court of Virginia</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Each type of court has a distinct jurisdiction and handles different types of cases. The Newport News Circuit Court is one of Virginia’s circuit courts, which means it has a broad jurisdiction and hears a variety of different types of cases.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>The History of the Newport News Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court has a long and storied history that stretches back to the earliest days of the Commonwealth of Virginia. The court was originally established in 1896 as part of the city’s efforts to create a more centralized and efficient judicial system. Over the years, the court has grown and evolved to meet the changing needs of the community it serves.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>The Structure of the Newport News Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court is part of Virginia’s 7th Judicial Circuit, which also includes the circuit courts of Hampton, Williamsburg, and James City County. The court is presided over by one judge, who is elected by the Virginia General Assembly to an eight-year term.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The court is supported by a number of other staff members, including clerks, bailiffs, and other administrative personnel. These individuals work together to ensure that the court runs smoothly and efficiently.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>The Functions of the Newport News Circuit Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court has a broad jurisdiction and hears a variety of different types of cases, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Civil cases with claims greater than $25,000</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Felony criminal cases</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Juvenile criminal cases transferred from the Juvenile and Domestic Relations District Court</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Appeals from the General District Court and Juvenile and Domestic Relations District Court</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Various other types of cases as authorized by law</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>The court also has a number of other important functions, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Administering oaths and affirmations</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Issuing marriage licenses</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Registering deeds and other legal documents</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Collecting fines and fees</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News General District Court:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News General District Court is a lower court that hears cases such as traffic violations, misdemeanors, and small claims disputes. The court is located at 2500 Washington Ave in Newport News, Virginia.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News-<a href=\"/blog/what-is-civil-court\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Civil Court\">Civil Court</a> Case Information:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Information about civil court cases heard in Newport News can be accessed through the Virginia Judiciary’s online case information system. This system allows individuals to view information about civil cases, including case status, court dates, and case documents.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News Circuit Court Phone Number:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The phone number for the Newport News Circuit Court is (757) 926-3601. This phone number can be used to contact the court for general inquiries or to speak with a specific department or staff member.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>see also <strong>Yuba County Superior Court</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News Circuit Court Hours:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court is open Monday through Friday from 8:00 am to 4:00 pm. The court is closed on weekends and on state holidays.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News Circuit Court Case Information:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Information about cases heard in the Newport News Circuit Court can be accessed through the Virginia Judiciary’s online case information system. This system allows individuals to view information about civil, criminal, and traffic cases, including case status, court dates, and case documents.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News General District Court Phone Number:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The phone number for the Newport News General District Court is (757) 926-3602. This phone number can be used to contact the court for general inquiries or to speak with a specific department or staff member.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News Juvenile Court:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Juvenile Court is a court that handles cases involving minors. The court is located at 2500 Washington Ave in Newport News, Virginia.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Newport News Circuit Court Judges:</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court has multiple judges who preside over cases in the court. The current judges are Honorable H. Vincent Conway Jr., Honorable Timothy S. Fisher, Honorable David F. Pugh, and Honorable Bryant L. Sugg.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The judges of the Newport News Circuit Court are responsible for presiding over a wide range of cases, including criminal, civil, and family law cases. They are appointed by the Virginia General Assembly and serve eight-year terms.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In addition to the judges, the Newport News Circuit Court has a number of other staff members who play important roles in the court’s operation. These staff members include clerks, bailiffs, and other administrative personnel.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you have a case that needs to be heard by the Newport News Circuit Court, it’s important to understand the court’s procedures and guidelines. You should consult with an attorney who can advise you on the appropriate steps to take and help you navigate the legal system.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Whether you’re involved in a criminal case, civil lawsuit, or family law matter, the Newport News Circuit Court is an important institution that plays a vital role in the administration of justice in Newport News, Virginia.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court is an important part of Virginia’s judicial system, with a long history and a broad jurisdiction. Whether you’re a resident of Newport News or simply curious about the state’s legal system, it’s important to have a basic understanding of this court and its functions. By familiarizing yourself with the Newport News Circuit Court, you can better understand the legal processes and procedures that shape our society.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>see also <a href=\"/blog/moore-county-district-court-detailed\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Moore County District Court\">Moore County District Court</a></p>\n\n\n\n<h2>FAQs</h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What types of cases does the Newport News Circuit Court hear?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court hears a variety of different types of cases, including civil cases with claims greater than $25,000, felony criminal cases, juvenile criminal cases transferred from the Juvenile and Domestic Relations District Court, appeals from the General District Court and Juvenile and Domestic Relations District Court, and various other types of cases as authorized by law.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Who presides over the Newport News Circuit Court?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court is presided over by one judge, who is elected by the Virginia General Assembly to an eight-year term.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What is the jurisdiction of the Newport News Circuit Court?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Newport News Circuit Court has a broad jurisdiction.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What is the role of the staff members in the Newport News Circuit Court?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The staff members of the Newport News Circuit Court play an important role in ensuring that the court runs smoothly and efficiently. This includes clerks, bailiffs, and other administrative personnel.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>What are some of the other functions of the Newport News Circuit Court?</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>In addition to hearing cases, the Newport News Circuit Court also has a number of other important functions, such as administering oaths and affirmations, issuing marriage licenses, registering deeds and other legal documents, and collecting fines and fees.</p>\n",
